# lab/profiles/adversarial.env — deliberately trap-laden inputs.
#
# Scenario defaults (test.lan / TEST / P@ssword123456!) are cooperative:
# alpha-only realm, short uppercase NetBIOS, password without quoting
# hazards. Cooperative inputs let several real bugs hide for weeks in
# the smb-proxy-appliance sibling (see dev-commons HANDOFF.md). This
# profile swaps in inputs that fight implicit assumptions in
# samba-sconfig provision-new and the scenario verify steps.
#
# What each swap traps for:
#
#   SC_REALM='example-shop.lan'
#     A realm with a hyphen. Hyphens are valid in DNS labels but some
#     scripts mangle them (greedy regex, BASH parameter expansion that
#     splits on '-'). The provisioned smb.conf realm value, the
#     realm-derived BASE_DN ("DC=example-shop,DC=lan"), the krb5.conf
#     default_realm, and the SYSVOL path
#     /var/lib/samba/sysvol/example-shop.lan/Policies/ all need to
#     preserve the hyphen exactly. Catches "${realm//[-.]/_}"-style
#     transformations that should NOT have been applied.
#
#   SC_NETBIOS='LONGFORESTNETB'   (15 chars exactly)
#     The NetBIOS name length boundary. NetBIOS 16-byte names use 1
#     byte for the suffix, leaving 15 visible chars. A 15-char name
#     should provision without truncation; a 16-char name SHOULD be
#     rejected at input validation. This profile picks the boundary
#     value to confirm the boundary itself isn't off-by-one.
#
#   SC_PASS=$'P@ss"word$with`backtick!\\and\047quote'
#     A password containing chars that are quoting hazards in shell
#     pipelines: double quote, $, backtick, backslash, single quote.
#     Catches places where the password is interpolated into an
#     unquoted ssh command, an eval, or a heredoc with parameter
#     expansion. The provision step pipes this through `kinit`, `net
#     ads`, and at least one whiptail prompt — all of which have
#     historically had quoting bugs in the smb-proxy sibling
#     (cf. fd4701f's bash 3.2 + ssh-quoting bug).
#
#   SC_FWD='10.10.10.1'
#     Unchanged from default — the lab forwarder is what it is and
#     varying it isn't an adversarial trap, it's just lab breakage.
#
# Usage:
#   lab/run-scenario.sh provision-new --profile adversarial
#
# What this profile does NOT cover (by design):
#   - Realms with multiple labels deeper than 2 (e.g. a.b.c.example).
#     That's a different test, not an "adversarial" one.
#   - Password collisions with shell metacharacters that are NOT
#     quoting hazards (e.g. literal newline in password). The default
#     ssh transport doesn't survive newlines anyway; that's an input
#     validation concern, not a quoting trap.

export SC_REALM='example-shop.lan'
export SC_NETBIOS='LONGFORESTNETB'
export SC_PASS=$'P@ss"word$with`backtick!\\and\047quote'
